// A REAL INSPECT DOCUMENT, CAPTURED, NOT DESIGNED. `docker inspect gunbc-glm53-stair-tp4` on srv7 during
// Group A fp8-8 launch 37175686123 (2026-10-04T04:25Z), 17679 bytes, git blob
// a87582f3f7d386840687322b60e5e30e5828fcf1, verbatim; its 35 Config.Env assignments were read and carry no
// secret. It is the next-rung trigger of gunbc.recurring_failure_mode
// a_comparator_read_the_inspect_field_its_producer_never_writes and
// a_readback_treated_image_inherited_environment_as_unplanned: the comparator is checked against what the
// daemon actually writes for this renderer, not against a document rendered from the plan.
// TWO VERBATIM PROJECTIONS OF THAT ONE DOCUMENT, each carrying only the top-level members its claim's
// subject reads (Id, Created, Image, Name, State, plus HostConfig for the mounts claim and Config.Env/Cmd
// for the environment claim); every value is byte-for-byte the captured one. Decoding the whole 17679-byte
// document per claim cost ~170k eval steps against the 72300 new-witness budget, paid for members
// (GraphDriver, NetworkSettings, Args, paths) no claim inspects.
